  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 430.000000px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": "Actually viewed the whole core sheet and fresh aha single on both native mattes, all 9 selected poses plus adopted neutral on 5 inherited 430 px pages, and all 7 decoded recipe rows. Broad round brown head, tan mottling, pale muzzle and belly, white eye surround with brown pupils, two rounded forelimbs, two feet and one short tapering side tail match the fixed identity. The mottled edges and paper texture are intentionally soft within bounded anatomy, not stray dirty pigment. Closed blink preserves the usual head/torso/foot positions closely. Greeting and left/right presentations use the proper existing forelimb with corresponding gaze; think brings a rounded paw to chin. Fresh aha retains a compact round paw with simple digit lines rather than the rejected human pointing finger, and has clean attachment to its shoulder. Cheer has two connected raised paws and intentional open smile/closed happy eyes. Species phases gently change the same tail curve. Facial lines, toes and outline remain clear at 430 px. No double anatomy, detached limb, transparency hole, edge cut, broad alpha color field or dirty isolated color patch was seen; all discrete recipes return to the exact adopted neutral.",
  "cautions": [
    "Native/max-size composites and decoded discrete strips were inspected; real-time playback, interpolation, final MP4 and physical UI zoom/density remain unverified."
